# PASS baseline is bounded finite geometry with normalized winding and semantic parts
# PASS mesh is deterministic and does not mutate a draft
# PASS standard chassis has full track loops, individual links, wheels, muzzle and fittings
# PASS drive_mobile visibly changes geometry in its named component part
# PASS protection_heavy visibly changes geometry in its named component part
# PASS protection_active visibly changes geometry in its named component part
# PASS armament_heavy visibly changes geometry in its named component part
# PASS sensors_integrated visibly changes geometry in its named component part
# PASS comms_data visibly changes geometry in its named component part
# PASS heavy chassis has larger width, longer hull and additional running gear
# PASS fully upgraded concept stays inside the renderer geometry budget
# PASS missing and unsupported values use stable safe visual defaults
# PASS browser global exports the same build contract without dependencies
# PASS every independent catalogue specification survives model resolution and GLB metadata
# PASS light chassis, casemate and separate exterior upgrades produce different valid meshes
